text.section:
The only objections to permits or permit modifications that may be raised by a surface owner are:

The operations plan for soil erosion and sediment control is not adequate or not effective;


Measures in addition to the requirement for a well's water-protection string are necessary to protect freshwater-bearing strata;


The permitted work will constitute a hazard to the safety of any person;


Location of the coalbed methane well or coalbed methane well pipeline will unreasonably infringe on the surface owner's use of the surface, so long as a reasonable alternative site is available within the unit and granting the objection will not materially impair any right contained in an agreement, valid at the time of the objection, between the surface owner and the operator or their predecessors or successors in interest; and


If the surface owner is an interstate park commission, the location of the well or pipeline will unreasonably infringe on the surface owner's use of the surface, so long as a reasonable alternative site is available within the unit and granting the objection will not materially impair any right contained in an agreement, valid at the time of the objection, between the surface owner and the operator or their predecessors or successors in interest.
